{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia","id":594736,"title":"Spirits, fomori, and the chosen of gaia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T07:40:35-07:00","id":594736,"title":"Spirits, fomori, and the chosen of gaia","content":"I've been looking through the internet for a while to find rules for non-fomori spirit hybrids and well.... I got nothing.<br /> <br /> It's not that they don't exist, I've found a plethora of references to other spirit possessed(Drones for the weaver, Gorgons for the wyld, and Kami for gaian spirit ridden). The problem is that they reference cWOD books I don't have and Don't have a snowballs chance in H*** of finding. Though many of them have suggested using the rules for standard spirit powers and ranking, which makes sense, spirit ridden are basically living fetishes.<br /> <br /> That unfortunately leads to a second problem, I can't find anything on cWOD spirit rankings, stats, or how influence works. Whenever I try looking this crap up it always points me to the nWOD book of spirits, which is useless to me. If I were to try using the rules for spirit combat and powers cWOD WTA and the ranking system of Book of spirits, all spirits would be OP as hell.<br /> <br /> So can anyone please, PLEASE give me a breakdown of the spirit ranking system and how to treat gnosis, rage, and &quot;power&quot; as the classic world of darkness uses it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T07:52:48-07:00","id":594752,"title":"","content":"Would there be any difficulty for you in buying <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2381/Possessed\" target=\"_blank\">Possessed</a> (which covers drones, gorgons and kami, as well as fomori) from DriveThruRPG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T08:07:12-07:00","id":594758,"title":"","content":"In ascending order, the Spirit Hierarchy/Ranking of W:tA (it's actually in the core book, incidentally) is as follows:<br /> <br /> Gafflings<br /> Jagglings<br /> Incarnae<br /> Celestines<br /> Supernals (The Triat)<br /> Gaia<br /> <br /> Stats can vary considerably. Gafflings tends to have lower stats, but this isn't guaranteed absolutely, while jagglings can have incredibly high stats, like ten (or in the case of some avatars to the Incarnae or particularly weird spirits, higher than that) in Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower and sometimes unique or semi-unique Charms, like the reality-warping capacity of a Nexus Cralwer or the fear aura of an Incarna's war-avatar. At the point where you reach Incarnae, spirits don't have meaningful stats anymore; they're generally gods in a single domain, or in the case of Celestines, many domains under a single concept. Supernals number three, are above Celestines, and constitute the Triat. Gaia is above them, as the spirit of all things; some place her under the Triat, but mainline Werewolf treats this as strictly optional and not the presentation that everything references.<br /> <br /> I'd advise getting a pdf of Possessed, if you can. It sets up four examples that would be really helpful to reference, and pdf isn't subject to horrible scalping costs like what I just saw on Amazon after a quick search. Dharma Book: Devil-Tiger also has a guideline for how many powers to give to a fomor based on what at the time was the second edition power rating (one for every ten points), which in Revised and on terms would be more like one power for every five points of Essence or so. Note that these powers would be taken from the sample list for NPC versions of these beings, rather than the specifically-weighted versions in Possessed or Freak-Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:23:48-07:00","id":594826,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf 20 Umbra book has a rather nice section on Kami. The book of the Wyld as well as Weaver have sections on Drones and Gorgons. But Possessed is hands down the best book on the subject of Formori, and company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:51:09-07:00","id":594893,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Are there any books detailing spirit ranks and progression(for lack of a better example) like the new world of darkness &quot;Book of Spirits&quot;. I haven't found anything that detail spirit powers and stats as defined in the 1-5 dot system for players/1-10 dot system for bosses and NPCs that everything else in cWOD use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T12:49:46-07:00","id":594918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=594893#post594893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Are there any books detailing spirit ranks and progression(for lack of a better example) like the new world of darkness &quot;Book of Spirits&quot;. I haven't found anything that detail spirit powers and stats as defined in the 1-5 dot system for players/1-10 dot system for bosses and NPCs that everything else in cWOD use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are detailed in the Werewolf core book (presently, W20), along with the basics of the Umbra. Their stats consist entirely of Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, with a fuel stat of Essence and a list of Charms. As noted, Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower work on the same 1-10 scale that they do for other stats of the type, except in certain circumstances, like Fenris's war-avatar (Rage 20 and Willpower 15) or the Daughters of Styx from Axis Mundi (Gnosis 17). Unlike Garou, Fera, and other non-spirit beings with these stats, they use them for everything. With possession, however, pretty much everything is dealing with the altered host and not the tenant, so these Traits won't really matter as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:14:47-07:00","id":595013,"title":"","content":"^Wait, so you're telling me that spirits, as opposed to mages, vampires, and werewolves, don't have a 1-5 limiter on their powers like ar\u00eate/generation/rank. On top of that their powers aren't limited by ranks like demons and wraiths, so they can learn any charm or gift they damn well please as long as they threaten/eat the right spirit? As well as store as much &quot;Essence&quot; as they want? That's a bit.... OP as hell.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the fact that spirits(as stated in the WTA player's guide) can create physical bodies using essence alone (1 essence per dot in strength/stamina/dexterity(limit 10 in each), 1 essence per 2 dots in abilities(limit 10 in each), 1essence for a base of 7 health levels and a cost of 1 essence per additional level(no limit), roll gnosis for mental and social rolls, and 1 essence per weaponry(aggravated). Also, as I have the books next to my desk, I've found 2 more examples of spirits with higher than 10 stats. See abba-il-aeon and umbrood lord lady Beloia in the book of madness, the former has a gnosis of 25 and a willpower of 20, the later has a gnosis of 12.<br /> <br /> Who was in charge of balancing this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:42:38-07:00","id":595022,"title":"","content":"No one, because it isn't to be balanced. Spirits aren't PCs. They're there for the ST to do what he needs to do. And believe, me, when some of those things have to be a chalenge to 5 to a dozen archmages or Rank 5 werewolfs, the last thing a ST needs is a dumb rule saying he have to limit himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:47:32-07:00","id":595025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595013#post595013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^Wait, so you're telling me that spirits, as opposed to mages, vampires, and werewolves, don't have a 1-5 limiter on their powers like ar\u00eate/generation/rank. On top of that their powers aren't limited by ranks like demons and wraiths, so they can learn any charm or gift they damn well please as long as they threaten/eat the right spirit? As well as store as much &quot;Essence&quot; as they want? That's a bit.... OP as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence is typically the sum of their other traits, and their Charms are typically limited, without much, if any, room for expansion. Note that combat for spirits is resolves by rolling Willpower to hit, Rage for damage, and depending on the rules set, Willpower or Rage to soak. It's not quite as great as you're thinking, though under Revised (not W20), Rage was the difficulty on damage rolls for attacks against spirits. Given the number of spirits with Rage 10, it didn't work out so well, and got removed in W20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention the fact that spirits(as stated in the WTA player's guide) can create physical bodies using essence alone (1 essence per dot in strength/stamina/dexterity(limit 10 in each), 1 essence per 2 dots in abilities(limit 10 in each), 1essence for a base of 7 health levels and a cost of 1 essence per additional level(no limit), roll gnosis for mental and social rolls, and 1 essence per weaponry(aggravated). Also, as I have the books next to my desk, I've found 2 more examples of spirits with higher than 10 stats. See abba-il-aeon and umbrood lord lady Beloia in the book of madness, the former has a gnosis of 25 and a willpower of 20, the later has a gnosis of 12.<br /> <br /> Who was in charge of balancing this? </div> </div> </div>There's some confusion here. You clearly cited rules from before Revised, since spirits don't spend Power (not Essence, that's under the newer system) to build a body. They just use the same stats and systems for spirits while material. Gnosis needs to be equal to or higher than the local Gauntlet to remain material, though. There are no Attributes to build up, or Abilities to buy, or weaponry to make. Those things are no longer a factor.<br /> <br /> As for spirits marked Umbrood, that's a strictly Mage term, though anything given a noble title or the rank of &quot;Aeon&quot; is going to be high up on the ranking for Mage and, accordingly, doing weird things. Can't really offer too much help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:07:25-07:00","id":595048,"title":"","content":"^Is 20th anniversary before or after revised addition, because that's the version I have in front of me. Also I'm referring to both WTA and the book of madness, so does that mean the werewolf and mage rules for spirit are different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T15:24:46-07:00","id":595061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595048#post595048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^Is 20th anniversary before or after revised addition, because that's the version I have in front of me. Also I'm referring to both WTA and the book of madness, so does that mean the werewolf and mage rules for spirit are different?</div> </div> </div> </div>The order is First - &gt; Second - &gt; Revised/3rd - &gt; 20th Anniversary Edition (W20). Werewolf has always had spirits with Charms, while Mage had spirits with Sphere effects and Arete before switching over to a different system, though I'm not really familiar with those details. Generally, though, if you're working with something for Werewolf, it's a good idea to completely disregard everything in every Mage book ever, because the two games aren't made to be played together without one getting thrown under the bus. So my advice to you, unless you plan on going the other way and diving into Mage, is to put the Book of Madness to the side and forget about it for the time being.<br /> <br /> It's curious that you say you have the Revised version in front of you, though, because the system that you quoted for materializing is from before it, and mentioned one of the earlier player's guides up thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:12:09-07:00","id":595649,"title":"","content":"^yeah sorry. I have multiple copies of different books and get them confused sometimes. I was experimenting with mechanics at the time to see if I could create a more balanced version of the material form charm( I know the official name is &quot;Materialize&quot;, but I call it material form so I don't get it confused with &quot;Appear&quot;, a charm with a similar name and effects.). I just started getting incredibly confused when I noticed some books referenced &quot;Essence&quot; as the power source for spirits while others referenced &quot;power&quot;. I guess it was just a simple version mix up.<br /> <br /> Also, off topic question question. What happens to a Fomori if a bane stops being just a tenant and takes full control of the body? For instance if it possessed a dead body and/or zombie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:57:37-07:00","id":595681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595649#post595649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^yeah sorry. I have multiple copies of different books and get them confused sometimes. I was experimenting with mechanics at the time to see if I could create a more balanced version of the material form charm( I know the official name is &quot;Materialize&quot;, but I call it material form so I don't get it confused with &quot;Appear&quot;, a charm with a similar name and effects.). I just started getting incredibly confused when I noticed some books referenced &quot;Essence&quot; as the power source for spirits while others referenced &quot;power&quot;. I guess it was just a simple version mix up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Also ,to add onto the pile of confusing terms, if you dig up any Kindred of the East books and see a Chi rating, that's equivalent to Power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, off topic question question. What happens to a Fomori if a bane stops being just a tenant and takes full control of the body? For instance if it possessed a dead body and/or zombie. </div> </div> </div>The process of wrangling control is covered in Possessed. Fomori, Drones, and Gorgons have an Autonomy rating to reflect how in control the original host part is. Giving up Autonomy nets you new powers without suffering from Taints, and it's the only way that Drones can get more powers. At Autonomy 0, the spirit pretty much wears through the flesh and becomes a normal spirit. At low Autonomy levels, the spirit will be mostly in control but not totally. Zombie reanimation is a bit of a different bag than most forms of possession, but it can be sort of had by a type of bane that turns the host into a zombie-like creature that can make a limited number of others rise up. There's an example of such a fomor in W20 Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T08:58:00-07:00","id":595683,"title":"","content":"@Saur Ops Specialist<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In ascending order, the Spirit Hierarchy/Ranking of W:tA (it's actually in the core book, incidentally) is as follows:<br /> <br /> Gafflings<br /> Jagglings<br /> Incarnae<br /> Celestines<br /> Supernals (The Triat)<br /> Gaia </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of debate whether Gaia is above or below the triat. One could say that Gaia literally is the world, raising her above everything else - or one could say that she is part of creation and thus affected by the whole creation/preservation/destruction cycle, which would place her within the power of the triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:01:23-07:00","id":595684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595683#post595683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Saur Ops Specialist<br /> It's a matter of debate whether Gaia is above or below the triat. One could say that Gaia literally is the world, raising her above everything else - or one could say that she is part of creation and thus affected by the whole creation/preservation/destruction cycle, which would place her within the power of the triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The debate isn't the default state of affairs, though. The writing never supports it as a real possibility in official materials; as far as the setting is concerned, Gaia is everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:19:46-07:00","id":595700,"title":"","content":"While I can't point towards a specific source right now, I'm fairly certain that the debate <i>is</i> occuring ingame (depending on how liberal the listeners are with regards to borderline-heretical thoughts) and I haven't yet read anything that conclusively places Gaia at the top. After all, if she is without a doubt the more powerful one, how come this whole Apocalypse-business is still a thing?<br /> <br /> Could you give me a source for Gaia being placed at the top without a doubt? Because W20 notes on page 307 that Gaia is not the entirety of the Tellurian and on page 321 that &quot;many claim that She's more than a Celestine, even though Her most comprehensible aspect takes the form of one&quot; - which means that it isn't even unambiguous that she's not &quot;simply&quot; a Celestine, wheras the following chapter on the triat begins with &quot;Three forces form the whole of creation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:53:50-07:00","id":595747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595700#post595700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can't point towards a specific source right now, I'm fairly certain that the debate <i>is</i> occuring ingame (depending on how liberal the listeners are with regards to borderline-heretical thoughts) and I haven't yet read anything that conclusively places Gaia at the top. After all, if she is without a doubt the more powerful one, how come this whole Apocalypse-business is still a thing?<br /> <br /> Could you give me a source for Gaia being placed at the top without a doubt? Because W20 notes on page 307 that Gaia is not the entirety of the Tellurian and on page 321 that &quot;many claim that She's more than a Celestine, even though Her most comprehensible aspect takes the form of one&quot; - which means that it isn't even unambiguous that she's not &quot;simply&quot; a Celestine, wheras the following chapter on the triat begins with &quot;Three forces form the whole of creation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That feels like bits of Mage creeping intrusively into Werewolf. In any case, 307 also states<br /> <br /> [quote = W20]...<b>all of the living parts of <u>creation</u></b> collectively form Gaia, whether they're in the physical world or beyond it.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Note that the same word for the cosmic chunk - creation - is used in the Triat description you cite. In any case, the entry at 321 likely has an important metatextual reason for mentioning Gaia before the Triat, given the focus of the game. And the core thesis is more important than the in-character quibbling in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T09:56:31-07:00","id":595751,"title":"","content":"From what I know, it may be a matter of debate more in line with mage games, but in werewolf games just mentioning it would be an act of heresy punishable by death (like everything in werewolf, I've gotten killed because my character dropped a McDonald's burger wrapper in one of the cairns)<br /> <br /> Also how should I handle supernatural fomori (like black spiral dancer or Baali Fomori) and/or non-triatic possessions (If bob the unaligned spirit possesses random guy A, do I use fomori, Kami, or a different set of rules)? As I was looking through spirit rules one of my friends recommended Freaks Legion as a reference to possessing and creating Fomori, but I'm wondering if it's up to date. I've only just recently downloaded Possession from Drivethrurpg and so far I haven't found anything on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T10:21:15-07:00","id":595760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595751#post595751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I know, it may be a matter of debate more in line with mage games, but in werewolf games just mentioning it would be an act of heresy punishable by death (like everything in werewolf, I've gotten killed because my character dropped a McDonald's burger wrapper in one of the cairns)</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be some context missing from the burger wrapper story, perhaps, but throwing trash in a sacred place is never appreciated. Churchgoers would take a dim view of it and at least a few humans might think that you should be killed. Garou have very real and memorable deals with spirits to keep that sort of thing from happening and will go from thinking to doing because you jeopardized the trust that they built up with the spirits, and also because Rage, aided along by Respect the Territory of Another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also how should I handle supernatural fomori (like black spiral dancer or Baali Fomori) and/or non-triatic possessions (If bob the unaligned spirit possesses random guy A, do I use fomori, Kami, or a different set of rules)? As I was looking through spirit rules one of my friends recommended Freaks Legion as a reference to possessing and creating Fomori, but I'm wondering if it's up to date. I've only just recently downloaded Possession from Drivethrurpg and so far I haven't found anything on the subject. </div> </div> </div>Don't bother with Freak Legion; the only thing it has are some additional powers and taints, and, well, one of the former is quite prurient. FL came out a long time before Possessed, incidentally, and lacks the system of Autonomy, which itself could use a bit of tweaking.<br /> <br /> Supernatural fomori are covered in W20 Book of the Wyrm, and it's mostly a list of complications or beings that can't be possessed. For unaligned spirits, pick the type that most closely resembles what you imagine happening to the host in question. Powers will occasionally be restricted by type, so what you want the host to do once the tenant is inside can potentially act as a guide for it. You might also try to mix and match certain setups based on those tendencies, like some spirit of grotesque nature that demands obedience and nothing else, using fomori-availability for powers and Drone Autonomy. However, everything in Werewolf ends up aligned whether it wants to be or otherwise, so there may be some strong pings on gifts that sense triatic taint.<br /> <br /> (Vampires can't usually be possessed except by blood banes and psychomachiae; Garou and Fera usually can't be possessed except by a certain type of bane and some Fera are completely immune, mages get a raw deal where the bane merges with and corrupts their avatar, and changelings can't be possessed unless their fae soul is inactive)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T10:51:39-07:00","id":595773,"title":"","content":"^Okay thanks, I'll see if I can find the latest book of the wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for context with the wrapper thing, our storyteller came up with this house rule that for every in-game 10 hours we go without eating the difficulty of all stamina roles is increased by 1.( As our brave heroes make their way to the 5th generation Methuselah's lair for the final battle, they stop at the local chik-fil-a for lunch.*note this is a joke*). so what ended up happening is after we were attacked by sabbat at a local Mcdonalds, my character stuffed the wrapper into his pocket and transformed (I had that gift that lets you not destroy your cloths when you wolf out). After a night battle that resulted in a trashed burger joint, many dead sabat, and us fleeing into the night with the Men-in-Black on our tails. We run into the umbra and didn't stop until we managed to get back to our home cairn(which was run by an ahroun elder), and unbeknownst to me, our storyteller remembered I still had leftovers in my pocket and made a secret roll that ended with my character unknowingly dropping said wrapper. The elder assumed I'd littered a cairn (therefore dishonoring him in front of the spirits) and thus my young rank 2 galliard faced an old and powerful rank 5 Ahroun elder in a duel to the death. You can imagine how that went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T15:54:09-07:00","id":596227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595684#post595684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The debate isn't the default state of affairs, though. The writing never supports it as a real possibility in official materials; as far as the setting is concerned, Gaia is everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it might be. We get the largest amount of data on how the setting works in the Werewolf books, and we have to confess that the Garou are quite unreliable in any religious affairs. They are zealots and the only way they can operate is if their dogma is strong. The other breeds are the ones that open things to discussion, and in their pragmatism and irreverence we may glean a kernel of truth. It might be bollocks, of course, but I prefer to think that they may actually be at least partially right.<br /> <br /> For years now I've been ascribing to the concept that the Triat was above all, and that there were other Super-Celestines in the cosmos where completley different beings have been tasked by their Creator to guard them from the insanities of the Triat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T16:37:56-07:00","id":596278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595747#post595747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That feels like bits of Mage creeping intrusively into Werewolf. In any case, 307 also states<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> W20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<b>all of the living parts of <u>creation</u></b> collectively form Gaia, whether they're in the physical world or beyond it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the same word for the cosmic chunk - creation - is used in the Triat description you cite. In any case, the entry at 321 likely has an important metatextual reason for mentioning Gaia before the Triat, given the focus of the game. And the core thesis is more important than the in-character quibbling in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted before, the question of who's the largest power is both already present in previous editions and entirely academic. We know that Gaia isn't powerful enough to easily fix the triat and the triat isn't powerful enough to calcify/snuff out Gaia without a <i>long</i> fight. Considering the vast scales of power involved, that's probably as precise as we're going to get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T19:21:25-07:00","id":596410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595773#post595773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...didn't stop until we managed to get back to our home cairn(which was run by an ahroun elder), and unbeknownst to me, our storyteller remembered I still had leftovers in my pocket and made a secret roll that ended with my character unknowingly dropping said wrapper. The elder assumed I'd littered a cairn (therefore dishonoring him in front of the spirits) and thus my young rank 2 galliard faced an old and powerful rank 5 Ahroun elder in a duel to the death. You can imagine how that went.</div> </div> </div> </div>This story sounds like the ST was just being an ass. That chain of events should never happen in game. Even is everyone was in a bad mood (in and/or out of game), and the elder overreacted, the fight should absolutely not be to the death. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T23:16:47-07:00","id":596556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595773#post595773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and unbeknownst to me, our storyteller remembered I still had leftovers in my pocket and made a secret roll that ended with my character unknowingly dropping said wrapper. The elder assumed I'd littered a cairn (therefore dishonoring him in front of the spirits) and thus my young rank 2 galliard faced an old and powerful rank 5 Ahroun elder in a duel to the death. You can imagine how that went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jesus, killed over a piece of litter? Just pick it up, throw it in the proper receptacle, and if the spirits are pissed about it, the elders could have just had you perform a Rite of Contrition to placate the spirits. A piece of trash doesn't justify killing off a Garou when every soldier is needed to fight the Apocalypse War. Yeah, duels to the death happen, and even duels that aren't to the death still have &quot;accidental&quot; deaths, but this? No way can a competent ST justify killing off a PC over a piece of trash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=596410#post596410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This story sounds like the ST was just being an ass. That chain of events should never happen in game. Even if everyone was in a bad mood (in and/or out of game), and the elder overreacted, the fight should absolutely not be to the death.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. There are so many non-lethal ways this could have been resolved, especially without having to kill off a PC for something so ridiculous and petty. I mean, Holy Jeebus, even performing the Rite of the Jackal on you for a week (and for a piece of litter, even a day would be too excessive IMHO) would have been a more appropriate punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T03:49:14-07:00","id":596683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595773#post595773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for context with the wrapper thing, our storyteller came up with this house rule that for every in-game 10 hours we go without eating the difficulty of all stamina roles is increased by 1.( As our brave heroes make their way to the 5th generation Methuselah's lair for the final battle, they stop at the local chik-fil-a for lunch.*note this is a joke*). so what ended up happening is after we were attacked by sabbat at a local Mcdonalds, my character stuffed the wrapper into his pocket and transformed (I had that gift that lets you not destroy your cloths when you wolf out). After a night battle that resulted in a trashed burger joint, many dead sabat, and us fleeing into the night with the Men-in-Black on our tails. We run into the umbra and didn't stop until we managed to get back to our home cairn(which was run by an ahroun elder), and unbeknownst to me, our storyteller remembered I still had leftovers in my pocket and made a secret roll that ended with my character unknowingly dropping said wrapper. The elder assumed I'd littered a cairn (therefore dishonoring him in front of the spirits) and thus my young rank 2 galliard faced an old and powerful rank 5 Ahroun elder in a duel to the death. You can imagine how that went.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just dickery by the ST. It's a blatant way to murder your character for some perceived slight. The Elder could have scolded you and hit you over the head for it, heck he could have challenged you over it, but if he challenged you, you would get to pick how you will fight - as a gallilard you could have easily picked a storytelling or song contest. He would have probably beaten you at that too, considering how badass you need to be at rank 5, but at least you would have given as good as you have gotten.<br /> <br /> And while Garou do kill each other over stuff, this is definetley not something they'd kill each other over. Especially not within a Challenge, in which killign the Garou is strongly discouraged.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T07:06:09-07:00","id":596869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/594736-spirits-fomori-and-the-chosen-of-gaia?p=595751#post595751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I know, it may be a matter of debate more in line with mage games, but in werewolf games just mentioning it would be an act of heresy punishable by death</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in New England. Being able to argue both of these points of view is encouraged for Theurges 'round these parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}